 "notes": "Five blocks x three arms, every arm 36 ARS updates (two rounds of three branches x 4 updates with the frozen ranking, then 12 updates), 15 finalists plus four frozen controls on twelve fresh 128-case manifests (1,536 cases per policy). 4,641,049 charged starts of 4,900,000; 483 of 660 minutes; 817.6 M transitions; 20 controller-generation calls of 40 allowed (none needed a correction, no invalid slot), 49,014 tokens. PRIMARY (blocks as units, 4 df): LLM minus GRAMMAR +0.030, 95% interval [-0.017, +0.076]; per block +0.086, -0.001, +0.048, +0.018, -0.003. The interval contains zero and 0.05: INCONCLUSIVE; no LLM advantage is established. Arm means: FIXED 0.742, GRAMMAR 0.713, LLM 0.743. Neither search beats the fixed template spending its branches on stochastic continuations: GRAMMAR minus FIXED -0.028 [-0.099, +0.042], LLM minus FIXED +0.001 [-0.095, +0.097]. Every arm beats the R-106 root (0.572) by 0.14-0.17 (Holm-significant). No finalist qualifies against the frozen JOINT (0.801); R-118 scored 0.790. Block 4 is low for both search arms (0.645, 0.642) against 0.758 for FIXED. What the LLM chose: round 1, in all five blocks, the two blend-target edits (hold, midrange), citing the template's 12.7% success among fired episodes; round 2, boost_end event in all five plus schedule periodic (three blocks) or support_end event (two). What survived the frozen ranking: target midrange in three LLM finalists, support_end event in two; boost_end event, the edit aimed at the largest D-090 failure category, was never selected in the LLM arm. The grammar's finalists: trend conditions (three), midrange (one), periodic + trend (one), the unedited template (one). So the LLM's choices were sensible and consistent, the selected structures are small (12-13 parameters), and they bought nothing measurable over continued fitting of the template at this budget. Instrument note: selection ranks branches on 512 placements after 4 updates, where identical slots differ by up to 0.045 (smoke), so the ranking is noisy; this was the agreed, frozen rule. Deviations, all before any generation or training: (1) the first launch died in the smoke on an implementer bug (a four-edit probe structure, past the language's three-edit cap); fixed, tested, and charged 20,000 starts on relaunch. (2) Smoke-gate amendment (advisor consult call_00310; the advisor left continuation to the user, the implementer continued under the user's standing delegation): the four-identical-slot check, a fixed 0.03 the implementer had set, failed at 0.045; it was replaced by a noise-scaled bound (4 x sqrt(mean discordance / cases) = 0.065) and the saved smoke re-evaluated without new simulation; the original failed gate and the pre-amendment frozen configuration are kept; no consistent slot bias was found in the saved data, but one batch cannot exclude it. (3) The smoke allowance was exceeded (28,210 starts charged against 20,000). (4) Executed authority is reported as trigger counts, hold and extra-boost steps and the mean action change against the root action; the protocol's 'action difference against the identity-disabled edit at identical observations' was not computed. (5) The driver's ssh session dropped during the continuations; the driver itself ran on uninterrupted. Limits: five blocks (4 df); one frozen residual root; a 13-edit language in which the LLM and the grammar choose from the same small menu; at most two edits per structure; 20 path updates on the final structure."
